msgstr "Total number of captured images across all classes. The more and the more varied, the more robust the model. Rule of thumb: at least 30 images per class, in different positions and lighting."

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Beispiele <0/>"
msgstr "Examples <0/>"

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Wie oft das Modell während des Trainings durch alle Beispiele gelaufen ist. Mehr Epochen = mehr Lernzeit, aber bei zu vielen kann Überanpassung entstehen (Modell merkt sich Bilder statt Muster)."
msgstr "How often the model went through all examples during training. More epochs = more learning time, but too many can cause overfitting (the model memorises images instead of patterns)."

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
#: src/lib/components/training/ModelTab.svelte
msgid "Epochen <0/>"
msgstr "Epochs <0/>"

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Schrittweite pro Anpassung der Gewichte. Zu groß = das Training schwingt über, zu klein = es lernt kaum. 0.001 ist der Standardwert."
msgstr "Step size per weight update. Too large = training overshoots, too small = it barely learns. 0.001 is the default."

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
#: src/lib/components/training/ModelTab.svelte
msgid "Lernrate <0/>"
msgstr "Learning rate <0/>"

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Anzahl der Neuronen in der versteckten Schicht. Mehr = komplexere Muster lernbar, aber es braucht auch mehr Bilder, um nicht überanzupassen."
msgstr "Number of neurons in the hidden layer. More = more complex patterns can be learned, but it also needs more images to avoid overfitting."

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
#: src/lib/components/training/ModelTab.svelte
msgid "Hidden Units <0/>"
msgstr "Hidden units <0/>"

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Wie viele Beispiele pro Lernschritt gleichzeitig durchs Modell laufen. Kleiner = rauschiger, aber oft besser für kleine Datensätze."
msgstr "How many examples pass through the model at once per learning step. Smaller = noisier, but often better for small datasets."

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
#: src/lib/components/training/ModelTab.svelte
msgid "Batch-Größe <0/>"
msgstr "Batch size <0/>"

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Optimierer"
msgstr "Optimiser"

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
msgid "Algorithmus, der die Gewichte anpasst. Adam passt für die meisten Fälle, SGD ist robuster für große Datensätze, RMSProp für rauschige."
msgstr "The algorithm that adjusts the weights. Adam suits most cases, SGD is more robust for large datasets, RMSProp for noisy ones."

#: src/lib/components/training/ModelStats.svelte
#: src/lib/components/training/ModelTab.svelte
